Hi experts out there,
I'm trying to convert tons of data (as well as FORTRAN programs that 
analyze the data) from VAX VMS system to SUN Unix system. The reason for 
this is our VAX machine is not very reliable nowadays (it's aging). I'm 
wondering if there is any file structure (on UNIX especially SUN) that 
is similar to keyed data structure of VMS. These data files are about 
10-30 MB (yes megabytes) each and consist of variable number of blocks 
per keyID (or primary key). I can translate these data sequentially but 
it would be very slow if the program calls for the data at the end of 30 
MB data file. I just don't know how to cross the data over to SUN while 
maintaining the efficiency of keyed structure. (Mainly becuase I'm a 
stranger in UNIX, I guess.)

Any help/comments will be greatly appreciated. Please e-mail me.
Thanks in advance.

