>Hi experts out there,
>I'm trying to convert tons of data (as well as FORTRAN programs that 
>analyze the data) from VAX VMS system to SUN Unix system. The reason for 
>this is our VAX machine is not very reliable nowadays (it's aging). 

What kind of VAX+disks were you using? Have you considered buying/leasing a 
newer/faster/less-power-consuming/more-reliable other VAX or an Alpha box.

>wondering if there is any file structure (on UNIX especially SUN) that 
>is similar to keyed data structure of VMS. These data files are about 
>10-30 MB (yes megabytes) each and consist of variable number of blocks 

Are those perhaps RMS INDEXED files? (CHeck with DIRECTORY/FULL on one)
If so, I suppose you should check out the various C-ISAM packages out there.
You really should take the oppurtunity to investigate whether going for a
relational database is perhaps the right thing to do.
(Btw.. 10-30 Mb is not very big at all, even fits comfortable in
memory even on the smaller VAXen)

